{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the break of dawn, thou shalt arise and make thy way to the airport, where thy journey to Japan doth begin. Take heed, for the plane doth await no man nor woman.\n\n\nIn the land of the rising sun, thou shalt first alight in Tokyo, the bustling metropolis filled with wonders and delights. Spend the day exploring the city, taking in the sights and sounds of this vibrant place.\n\n\nThe following day, venture to the ancient city of Kyoto, the former imperial capital of Japan. Here, thou shalt find temples and shrines aplenty, each with its own unique story to tell.\n\n\nOn the third day of thy journey, travel to Hakone, a town nestled in the mountains known for its hot springs and views of Mount Fuji. Take a dip in the soothing waters and enjoy the natural beauty of this place.\n\n\nThe fourth day, return to Tokyo and visit the famed Tsukiji Fish Market. Witness the hustle and bustle of the early morning auction and sample the freshest sushi and sashimi.\n\n\nOn the fifth day, embark on a day trip to Nikko, a city located in the mountains north of Tokyo. Here, thou shalt find the Toshogu Shrine, a UNESCO World Heritage Site and the final resting place of Tokugawa Ieyasu, the founder of the Tokugawa shogunate.\n\n\nThe sixth day, journey to Hiroshima, a city with a tragic past but a bright future. Pay thy respects at the Peace Memorial Park and Museum, and reflect on the events of August 6, 1945.\n\n\nOn the seventh and final day, return to Tokyo and spend thy last day in Japan exploring the city's myriad offerings. Whether it be shopping, dining, or sightseeing, make the most of thy time in this wondrous land.\n\n\nAnd so, with a heavy heart, thou shalt bid farewell to Japan and begin the journey home, taking with thee memories that will last a lifetime. Fare thee well, Japan, and may we meet again.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logpr